From: Anonymous
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: Advertise HDMI 2.1 PCON support on DCN201

DCN201 is the only DCN2-class resource pool that leaves
dc->caps.dp_hdmi21_pcon_support at false. Without it the link layer never
attempts FRL negotiation with a DP 1.4 -> HDMI 2.1 protocol converter, so
a PCON adapter is driven as plain HDMI 2.0 TMDS and 4K120 is only
reachable at 4:2:0.

Author: TeleBooth, published at
https://gist.github.com/TeleBooth/d88ef745895d444a401d0e621de9818e
as bc250-dcn201-pcon-hdmi21.patch (the file itself is signed "Anonymous").
Tested by them and several other BC-250 owners at 3840x2160@120Hz 4:4:4 through a
Cable Matters 102101 PCON into an LG CX.

Carried here until it lands upstream.
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c
index 765c63513a31..2282fd493cdd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/resource/dcn201/dcn201_resource.c
@@ -1332,6 +1332,8 @@ static bool dcn201_resource_construct(
 
 	dc->caps.max_odm_combine_factor = 2;
 
+	dc->caps.dp_hdmi21_pcon_support = true;
+
 	dc->cap_funcs = cap_funcs;
 
 	return true;
